tmp_text "I'd be willing to have a look at fighter strength as soon as Iget up to a level where I can code.  I agree that guild code is moresensitive to changes than most \"normal\" code, but one possible solutionto the fighter problem is to just change some of their constants - givethem a better weapon, better armour, more attacks, better base AC etc.This should be relatively straightforward and would go a long waytoward alleviating a guildpower discrepancy.Katana the newbie(wiz)**I don't think it is unfair to give them back their heavy weapons.It is the only thing they have got. Bezerk they have from level 20It will cost 40 sp and they have two attacks and three attacks above 25.I also don't think it will be possible for a fighter to change guild,I think it is impossible to close the fightersguild. A fighter has onlyimproved his con,dex,str they are made for fighting. This guild isunique and should stay. I volunteer toguard the guild. That will say when portil took over the jedis i willdo the same to the fighters as i did with the jedis. Search for bugsand recode them where neccessary.Well arches let me know what you think of this.    Maybe GG (guild guard) of the fighters,                              Suicidal Gladiator.**Hello,Today i saw a player getting killed on a vicious hit he apparantlymade on himself.The monster he was fighting was _very_ heavy (shermans archdemon)and somehow the vicious hit was returned to himseld(himself) and killed him on impactKbl and I went over this case, and checked it out. The formula that gives a vicious hit is a bit strange in both my opinion and Kbl'sGerrit got the loss back on Exp, but this case will be looked afterYour's coffee-addicted Dice**Don't know when it was added but of course Gerrit died when he gota vicious hit:  the archdemon has a fireshield!  Gerrit shouldnot have been compensated...Meecham**This is definetly not a bug in the fighters guild. I looked the codeover and over at home but could not find a placewhere the could possibly return to the player himself. So if there is a bugof a fireshield it must be in the archde*excuses my keyboard S^ &$#@ * archdemon and not in the guild  Thank you,   Gladiator, looking after fighters guild**  It should be noted that the archdemon was not fireshielded last timeI paid him a visit (2.5 weeks ago, as I recall).  Unless there is somevery good reason to make this monster a whole lot tougher (in a questwhich is already very long in killing) I suggest someone with the authority to do so should remove the fireshield.Katana**ok. There have been alot of guild changes. I thinka summary posting of the should be placed here.The ones I know about for new GM's are:Jedi		ManglaFighter	PortilMonk		Warlord (I believe)Druid	Meecham (When Open)Please add to this list where appropriate.		Mangla**druids are almost done...anyone wanna write about 100 docs for me? *grin*Meech**Hmmm seems the ninjas sometimes have a problem in that thier skillswill not advance. They said some wizard jump started it lasttime.  My question is who and can we have the solution?*grin*			Mangla**Hello all :-(In some idle minutes i am a bit checking through the guilds...Today: vagabonds:    -timestop: Since the mages started, most guilds get a hold-spell               But this one is the most powerful, I checked it with               a level 1 monster and with a level 99 several times,              With both the hold spell worked about 15 !!!! rounds              This is ridiculous, Why not build an int-check on the              Monster to give it a savings-throw (total) and reduce               the hold accodring to the level.   -fasttalk: Same as above.... It words every time ??!!??              on level 1 monster as well on level 99.               It should be nearly impossible for a player to make              a lv 99 monster peacful.                      SourcerPS: I couldn't check if i simply had good luck testing this cause    Colossus secured his guild/lib directory where the soul is *shrug***Ok, barbarians this time :-((CLOSE THEM IMEDIATLY !!!!!They do 600 Damage in on round at will !!and it even costs no sp alt all !!!Check the bodyslam for that :-(((                SourcerPS: Has this mud gone crazy ????***There is a bug in thier quest weapon code. Seem that youdo not have to do the quest to get the weapon. This isalso in a secured dir so...If some nice arch has timebefore colossus gets back, like we all know he will soon,then could you please take a look at it or copy it somewherefor us lowly people to peruse?		Mangla**The barbarians were changed after Moonchild was banished.The values were rediculously high.Now I have put the original values back.G for HM**I had a complaint today about the summoner guild. (A Summoner agreed with me)It seems as though the Summoners get xp for the kill when two players are attacking the same monster nomatter who killed it...Players in question Gambit and Topaz.Portil**Ok, here are the stats:arch  ac:29     wc:30 !!!!  hp: +2000lord  ac:28    wc:29 !!    hp: +1800.... and so onThe wc of their monsters about 10 points higherthan the on of normal obj/monster, as well as the acAnd the golem give 'em about 3 times the HP a normal player (summoner) hasA normal summoner at level 20 has by this way:  ABOUT 1000   HP !!!!!!!!   2 ATTACKS per around, on with illigal WC !!!Ok, think about it !!        SourcerPS: A good idead would be to patch all player to summonercause no other guild is that powerful, not half of it**Summoners complained long ago that when their monsters killed somethingthe monster was getting the xp instead of them.  The problem with theSummoners getting all the xp is prolly caused by some quick fix Matt didto make sure that the summoner got the xp instead of their monster.Meech**Hi.	I am in the middle of re-writing some of the guild codeto reduce the power of the Summoners. As Holy Mission's guildsbecome stronger and weaker, it becomes necessary to try to balancethem. The summoners are as strong as they are because a short whileago, that power was required for guild balance. Now it seems thatthe balance has shifted to the Summoners, and rather than have otherguilds raise theirs and enter an escalation war, I will lower mine.Among the changes are \"stamina\" points for the Attackers, whichlimits the amount of time they can exist, and a global reduction inoverall power (spell power and duration, and Attacker stats). Thesechanges are already being written, just be patient and they willbe installed shortly.		- Matt**Greetings friends.  As most of you know, I lost MUD access for a while, but am now semi-backI have started working on Samurai guild on MS-DOS editor (Not MUD ready yet).I have written an overview in /p/e/guild/README.Please read it if you have time and tell me about your opinions.--ExosP.S. What are Barbarian and Vagabond guild??????????????**These are a few observations after reading the README file:Why do samurai get a 'Seppuko--Teleport back to guild'? How is it supposedto work? They run very fast and no one sees them???? I just do notunderstand WHY they should get it.Warshout? A hold spell in disguise????? Why not make it do something else?Like help your party members for a short while... Ie.Help them to fightfor your cause better.Whirlwind? Barbarians Melee???? It should only last a short while. Samuraiare not as strong willed as Barbarians and do not have the stamina. Sothe ability should not last long.Warscream - Remove the ability. It should not be there.About the Restrictions:No spells???? What are the abilities but spells in diguise. Therefore nota great drawback.No initiation of Player killings. Wow.... Great drawback.It is not based on just parts of the 1st edition Oriental Adventures,it comes from ALL of it.    Dancer in the Dreams of Fate.**I must apologize to Dancer and everyoner else.I am not at all familiar with barbarian guild.TO clarify:Whirlwind is but ONE attack......not like a berzerk or anything (and expensive)For Shout and Scream, I want to try them like the book, BUTThere is no real effect of increased strength in this MUD. In actual AD&D terms: Shout increases STR to 18/00 for 1 round;Scream increases STR to 18/00 for 2 rounds,and ALL enemies within 10' are stunned for the next round.I detect a bit of sarcasm against my anti-PK stand....I am trying to code Bushido into the guild....and that IS part of Bushido,it can be argued that there is NO PKing in HM, but from what I remember,PKing is very prevelant!!!!!!!!!!  (Is Cthulhu still around?)This clause prevents a SAMURAI from attacking anyother player for ANY reason.Finally, Seppuko:During Seppuko, a Samurai draws his blade and slashes open his stomach,while a companion decapitates him.  Ensuring death.  The game effect is a return to the guild (and confusing players....Why did he commit suicide?)The Samurai returns to the guild, but all in the area think he died...they even see a corpse.Wimpying from combat must either be disallowed or MUST end in Seppuko byBushido code. (Lifeblood of the Samurai)I must thank Dancer for looking at my files (I did not expect so quick of a response)Exos bows deeply to all of the powerful immortals on this mighty world.**Seppuko:Well if you are doing Seppuko as you have described in the note above, thenthe cost of it, should not be spell points, but Experience Points.I would suggest that for EACH use, they lose 10% of ALL their experience points.That way they are not losing all that they would with a death, but they dolose something.    Dancer in the Dreams of Fate.**"
